&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Philo is looking for a strategic, creative, and hands-on Head of Social Media to lead our organic social presence across entertainment, culture, and community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person will own social strategy, editorial planning, and platform-native content creation — bringing strong instincts in writing, filming, editing, design, and trend-driven execution. They’ll partner closely across Marketing, Design, Programming, Customer Support, Legal, and external creators to keep Philo’s social presence timely, consistent, and unmistakably Philo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Philo’s organic social strategy, editorial calendar, and channel approach across key platforms, with a strong focus on short-form video, Reels, Tiktok, YouTube Shorts, and emerging formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, film, edit, design, publish, and optimize platform-native social content, including video, graphics, memes, captions, carousels, and trend-driven posts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong creator/creative ethos to the role, understanding what makes content feel native, shareable, entertaining, and worth watching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop social campaigns around programming priorities, cultural moments, giveaways, partner needs, and audience-specific initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain Philo’s social voice and ensure content feels confident, approachable, audience-first, culturally aware, and unmistakably Philo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Design, Brand, Growth, Product Marketing, Customer Support, Legal, agencies, and external creators to bring social ideas to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support influencer and creator partnerships through creator sourcing, briefs, content review, and performance learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee community management, moderation, and escalation standards across social channels, Reddit, and app store reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data, community feedback, and audience insights to inform content, creative, and marketing recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in social media, content creation, entertainment marketing, brand marketing, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading organic social strategy, editorial planning, content development, publishing, and reporting for a consumer-facing brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on skills in filming, editing, short-form video, social design, meme creation, writing, and platform-native storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in short-form video, especially TikTok, Instagram Reels, and YouTube Shorts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a strong curiosity about trends and developments in the social media landscape including new and emerging platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio of social work that shows creative range, platform fluency, and content that has meaningfully driven engagement, reach, conversation, or cultural relevance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with tools like CapCut, Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, Figma, Sprout Social, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong creative instincts around TV, entertainment, pop culture, memes, fandom, creator culture, internet behavior, and what makes content shareable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent writing, editorial judgment, project management, and cross-functional collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with programming launches, partnerships, giveaways, cultural moments, community moderation, and creator/influencer collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
